1
00:00:01,040 --> 00:00:04,180
Now everybody lift your hands up!

2
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:06,261
Sing about what you are dreaming!

3
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:07,800
Always stand up!

4
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:09,977
Raise up the flag that can't be beaten!

5
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:11,500
Gotta keep up!

6
00:00:11,660 --> 00:00:13,997
We'll get past every
wall that's in our wake!

7
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:15,737
Go without hesitation!

8
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:16,860
Hands up!

9
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:26,617
We just have to press on a little more.

10
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,217
To get to the answers we're looking for.

11
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,737
We came to this new world believing that

12
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:37,917
surely someday we just might find the way.

13
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,897
All the pieces of our dreams
have now come together.

14
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:45,397
Our bonds won't waver.

15
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:47,837
With our dreaming hand.

16
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,920
Let's head on towards

17
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:52,717
a bright new future.

18
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:56,557
Now everybody lift your hands up.

19
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:58,557
Sing about what you are dreaming.

20
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:00,177
Always stand up.

21
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:02,417
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

22
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:03,957
Gotta keep up.

23
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,317
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

24
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,420
Let's head on never stopping.

25
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,377
Only look up.

26
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:13,397
Keep your head up. Way up high.

27
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:15,077
Always step up.

28
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:16,997
If waves erupt up to the sky.

29
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:19,417
Never give up. Our wishes.

30
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:20,757
They will come together.

31
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:21,977
And lead us on.

32
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:23,180
For the future.

33
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:26,217
We drift on.

34
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:27,837
Riding the waves.

35
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:29,457
Towards another shore.

36
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:30,717
Day by day.

37
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:33,337
There are many meetings.

38
00:01:33,420 --> 00:01:35,517
Many goodbyes.

39
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:37,820
Underneath the flag we fly.

40
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:42,457
I'll remember.

41
00:01:42,540 --> 00:01:45,877
The pain within, I'll keep
it in my heart forever.

42
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:49,837
And never take it lightly,
but I won't surrender.

43
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:54,597
This freedom, I will keep in mind,
I'll keep holding on, never stop it.

44
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:59,497
Now everybody lift your hands up,
sing about what you are dreaming.

45
00:01:59,580 --> 00:02:03,357
Always stand up, raise up
the flag that you believe in.

46
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:07,237
Gotta keep up, we'll get past
everyone that's in our way.

47
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:09,820
Let's head on, never stop it.

48
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:14,337
Only look up, keep your
head up when I'm high.

49
00:02:14,420 --> 00:02:17,937
Always step up, if waves are
rough, jump through the sky.

50
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:21,677
Never give up, our wishes
they will come together.

51
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:24,120
And lead us on towards our future.

52
00:02:24,980 --> 00:02:26,160
Hands up.

53
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:58,177
I've worn that thing with
some kind of passive beast.

54
00:02:58,260 --> 00:03:00,277
But when the hell has
Caesar ever been interested?

55
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:01,400
in human weapons?

56
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:02,680
Get me in range!

57
00:03:02,820 --> 00:03:04,160
Coming right up!

58
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:07,668
Whatever it is, he'll
regret shooting at us.

59
00:03:07,780 --> 00:03:10,133
If you wanted to fight, well here it is!

60
00:03:23,740 --> 00:03:25,017
General, and okay!

61
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:27,660
I didn't even put a dent in him!

62
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:32,820
General! Shield!

63
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:35,024
That's too little and too late!

64
00:03:35,820 --> 00:03:36,650
General!

65
00:03:36,733 --> 00:03:37,563
Shield!

66
00:03:37,646 --> 00:03:38,900
Thread through a shield?

67
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:40,295
Talk about desperate!

68
00:03:44,460 --> 00:03:45,290
Well, then.

69
00:03:45,373 --> 00:03:48,633
Looks like I'm just gonna have
to break out the big guns.

70
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:49,560
Sorry, pal.

71
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:52,297
As long as you're standing
between us and Caesar,

72
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:53,977
I'm afraid that makes you our enemy.

73
00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:55,820
Weapon Morphosis!

74
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:07,850
Esparagirl!

75
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:11,280
Good guy!

76
00:04:12,340 --> 00:04:13,380
Round and round!

77
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:14,800
Round and round!

78
00:04:19,420 --> 00:04:20,280
Shut up!

79
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:25,997
What were you saying about
no more getting sidetracked?

80
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:27,962
Time for a more direct approach.

81
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:32,680
Call me Missile Girl.

82
00:04:33,460 --> 00:04:34,620
Target is inside!

83
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:35,760
Ready, fire!

84
00:04:36,740 --> 00:04:38,317
Launching! Spin!

85
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:39,341
Projecto Cannon!

86
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:41,960
Caesar's coming with us!

87
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:43,120
Wait, Caesar?

88
00:04:43,460 --> 00:04:45,342
What are you even talking about?

89
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:05,860
Where the hell am I?

90
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:19,717
the heart of the leader
of the g5 what a wonderful

91
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:24,660
souvenir thanks with
this the fight is over

92
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:35,320
Smoker, your heart is still in my
hands, and I'm not going to hell alone.

93
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:44,397
What the hell are you Straw Hats
standing around and waiting for?

94
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:48,421
We can't let Caesar escape, or the
entire plan will be for nothing.

95
00:05:48,740 --> 00:05:50,400
All of you, get on now!

96
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,940
Sure we will, when we have everyone.

97
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:55,560
I'm waiting for my whole crew!

98
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:04,240
Run like your life depends on it!

99
00:06:04,340 --> 00:06:06,357
We're trying the best we can, Usopp!

100
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:10,100
You gotta move faster than the gas!

101
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:11,990
Hooray!

102
00:06:12,073 --> 00:06:13,117
The gate is starting to close!

103
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:15,740
Only 50 meters left,
then you're home free!

104
00:06:16,180 --> 00:06:17,415
We're going with you!

105
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:18,757
Whatever floats your boat!

106
00:06:18,840 --> 00:06:20,193
The gate's gonna close!

107
00:06:23,760 --> 00:06:24,600
They're here!

108
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:30,520
That was a close call!

109
00:06:30,860 --> 00:06:32,140
The crew's all here!

110
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:34,257
Were you trying to make us worry?

111
00:06:34,340 --> 00:06:35,580
I knew you'd make it!

112
00:06:35,820 --> 00:06:38,500
It was all thanks to
you, Usa! That's right!

113
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:40,524
We didn't see him carrying you!

114
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:42,680
Well, guys, you heard him!

115
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:45,500
No reason to wait around,
right? All aboard!

116
00:06:46,380 --> 00:06:48,640
Time to get out of here! Yeah!

117
00:06:50,900 --> 00:06:56,237
what about Kin'emon is there anything
we can do for him what that's Kin'emon

118
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:58,717
we're just gonna have to figure something

119
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:03,560
out later no what do they do to you

120
00:07:07,980 --> 00:07:10,120
Joker, are you there?

121
00:07:11,740 --> 00:07:12,570
Me.

122
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:15,520
Monet.

123
00:07:16,380 --> 00:07:17,210
Monet?

124
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:19,660
I'm surprised you're alive.

125
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,294
Vargo's been defeated.

126
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:25,600
Caesar as well.

127
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:30,105
Though Baby Five and Buffalo
should be able to recover him soon.

128
00:07:31,420 --> 00:07:33,840
I misjudged the whole situation.

129
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:43,060
Deep in the third lab,

130
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:47,257
you'll find the weapon responsible for
destroying the first two laboratories,

131
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:51,160
as well as the rest of the
island, exactly four years ago.

132
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:54,437
With the simple push of a button,

133
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:58,049
Punk Hazard's population will
be reduced to a single person.

134
00:07:58,660 --> 00:08:02,080
The only one who can survive
the land of the dead.

135
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:04,520
Our dear friend Caesar.

136
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:07,077
The location of the device...

137
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:09,631
You don't need to say another word, Joker.

138
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:13,560
I was going to do it anyway.

139
00:08:14,780 --> 00:08:17,360
Actually, I'm next to
the switch right now.

140
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:23,500
The explosion will sink
their only means of escape.

141
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:26,682
Just as long as you're
okay with losing a tanker.

142
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:27,820
Very good.

143
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:30,337
die for me.

144
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:33,420
Monda and take everything with you.

145
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:39,040
young master.

146
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:51,557
at the very least.

147
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:53,420
I'll get my revenge on you.

148
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:56,137
this is goodbye!

149
00:08:56,220 --> 00:08:59,980
I, sorry it had to end
like this, old friend.

150
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:07,260
Thank you, for your years of service.

151
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:43,420
Pretty hot, huh, this Missile
Girl's burning passion.

152
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:47,840
Hey, hey, baby, fly!

153
00:09:49,420 --> 00:09:51,497
You still want to hold on to this weapon?

154
00:09:51,580 --> 00:09:54,357
I mean, you can already turn
into every weapon you want.

155
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:55,617
Thanks for grabbing it, Buffalo.

156
00:09:55,700 --> 00:09:59,520
That was sweet, that weapons
imbued with magic powers, you know.

157
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:05,277
Whoever owns this weapon is
bound to lead a happy life,

158
00:10:05,360 --> 00:10:08,277
and if you buy it from me,
you'll make me a happy man, too.

159
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:14,757
That was just a scam obviously,

160
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:16,037
oh crap!

161
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:17,720
Look up behind you, baby!

162
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:27,960
Oh, Iron Pirate! Wow!

163
00:10:28,380 --> 00:10:30,740
I don't fight for peace on the sea!

164
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:32,496
Is that even for me?

165
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:34,330
No!

166
00:10:34,413 --> 00:10:35,243
Iron Pirate!

167
00:10:35,326 --> 00:10:36,182
Done with this.

168
00:10:36,460 --> 00:10:37,740
Weapon-morphosis!

169
00:10:38,420 --> 00:10:39,520
Revolver girl!

170
00:10:42,420 --> 00:10:44,160
Ha! That's it!

171
00:10:47,100 --> 00:10:48,720
This ought to do the job.

172
00:10:49,140 --> 00:10:50,140
Deflect this!

173
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:07,200
Why is there a dragon here with us?

174
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:10,680
Momo, I made him out of
garbage dump. Wow, what?

175
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:12,310
Father!

176
00:11:13,040 --> 00:11:14,746
This eel is quite distraught.

177
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:17,080
Please save my father!

178
00:11:18,940 --> 00:11:20,440
It's gone mad!

179
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:24,920
Momo, what's wrong?

180
00:11:41,280 --> 00:11:47,537
Every one of you, this is where
you will die here with me,

181
00:11:47,620 --> 00:11:50,877
though I won't be around to see it.

182
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:55,260
I know you'll become
the king of the pirates!

183
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:11,520
Hey, are you okay?

184
00:12:14,280 --> 00:12:15,997
I don't know what happened.

185
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:17,217
But that sounded pretty bad.

186
00:12:17,300 --> 00:12:19,124
Must have come from building D.

187
00:12:19,580 --> 00:12:20,717
Trust me, I know.

188
00:12:20,800 --> 00:12:22,300
That's the S .A .D.

189
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:23,558
Manufacturing Room.

190
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:32,830
Monet!

191
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:41,720
Hey, hello.

192
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:47,900
I was under the impression that my
heart was in Caesar's possession.

193
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:51,854
So how the hell did you end
up getting your hands on it?

194
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:55,569
Simply put, he got
mixed up on the details.

195
00:12:55,740 --> 00:12:58,200
I hold on to your heart for safekeeping.

196
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:02,300
He let me hold on to his
secretary Monet's heart.

197
00:13:02,560 --> 00:13:05,400
We have ourselves a deal,
shall we shake on it?

198
00:13:05,980 --> 00:13:10,640
And as you know, I sliced out your
heart when you first arrived at the lab.

199
00:13:18,480 --> 00:13:22,760
The heart of the leader of
the T5, Vice Admiral Smoker.

200
00:13:23,480 --> 00:13:25,220
What a wonderful souvenir.

201
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:27,150
Thanks.

202
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:32,577
He just made that assumption and
I didn't bother correcting him.

203
00:13:32,660 --> 00:13:35,601
But I gave him back Monet's
heart out of kindness.

204
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:38,240
I need a response.

205
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:44,600
As the old saying goes, when you do
something nice for other people...

206
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:48,821
Well, that good karma's
bound to come back to you.

207
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:56,100
Oh, crap!

208
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:58,753
This tunnel's gonna collapse any second!

209
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:01,100
I got it!

210
00:14:02,260 --> 00:14:04,378
The ceiling's completely giving out!

211
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:08,997
This tunnel is burrowed
directly through the mountains.

212
00:14:09,080 --> 00:14:10,727
The cave Zin will be buried.

213
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:13,193
You gotta do something about it or what?

214
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:17,630
Damn it!

215
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:19,160
The passage is blocked!

216
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:20,182
Hit the brakes!

217
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:36,360
Holy crap!

218
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:37,720
He saved us!

219
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:41,080
I don't want that guy as
my enemy, even if he is!

220
00:14:43,260 --> 00:14:46,201
There's bound to be a gas
cloud blocking the exit.

221
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:50,440
Anyone on board capable of
conjuring up some wind? What?

222
00:14:51,180 --> 00:14:54,457
You expect someone to just
coincidentally have that power?

223
00:14:54,540 --> 00:14:56,200
Oh, right here.

224
00:14:56,380 --> 00:14:58,460
I can do that. Seriously?

225
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:00,902
I can see the end of the tunnel!

226
00:15:02,880 --> 00:15:03,710
Nice.

227
00:15:03,793 --> 00:15:05,231
Just a little more to go.

228
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:06,720
Move faster!

229
00:15:14,060 --> 00:15:15,580
Where are you?

230
00:15:20,160 --> 00:15:22,140
I can't find the young master.

231
00:15:22,820 --> 00:15:25,520
He should be in his room
on the fourth floor.

232
00:15:26,640 --> 00:15:27,820
But he's not.

233
00:15:28,080 --> 00:15:29,180
I looked up there.

234
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:30,940
The window was open.

235
00:15:32,620 --> 00:15:34,180
Ah, well then.

236
00:15:35,540 --> 00:15:37,780
I don't know where he is.

237
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:46,600
Sounds like he headed
off on his own again.

238
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:50,990
It's me.

239
00:15:51,073 --> 00:15:53,118
Tell me what's happening over there.

240
00:15:54,520 --> 00:15:55,350
Actually.

241
00:15:55,433 --> 00:15:57,657
We got some kind of metal security guard.

242
00:15:57,740 --> 00:15:58,799
Giving us trouble.

243
00:16:00,940 --> 00:16:02,437
But other than that.

244
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:04,157
The two of you are still safe.

245
00:16:04,240 --> 00:16:05,440
Yes sir.

246
00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:09,477
All right, it's settled.

247
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:12,560
For now, I want you two to
take care of that guard.

248
00:16:15,300 --> 00:16:16,700
I'll be there shortly.

249
00:16:42,240 --> 00:16:43,070
Huh?

250
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:48,860
I am an Invincible Iron Palace!

251
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:54,190
Super!

252
00:16:56,180 --> 00:17:00,240
After an attack like that, even
a pacifista would be busted up.

253
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:02,180
Weapon Morphosis!

254
00:17:03,700 --> 00:17:06,020
Flying Sis Girl!

255
00:17:07,080 --> 00:17:09,020
Make his head spin!

256
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:16,220
Weapon Morphosis!

257
00:17:17,780 --> 00:17:19,280
Fire Girl!

258
00:17:25,100 --> 00:17:26,000
Ow!

259
00:17:26,220 --> 00:17:27,640
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

260
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:29,098
Hot, hot, hot, hot!

261
00:17:32,180 --> 00:17:33,900
No enemy, however strong,

262
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:37,517
is immune from the burning passion
of Firegirl's flame of love.

263
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:38,880
Fix that, Franky.

264
00:17:43,860 --> 00:17:45,220
General AMG!

265
00:17:46,140 --> 00:17:46,970
What?

266
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:50,300
Any fresh ideas?

267
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:52,012
He's one tough customer.

268
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:53,920
Bring it on!

269
00:17:54,180 --> 00:17:57,557
I'm ready for more, fan
man and weapon woman!

270
00:17:57,640 --> 00:18:00,160
Hey, baby, you think what I'm thinking?

271
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:04,237
We serve him up something special
that no one's ever been able to block.

272
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:05,560
Try your best.

273
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:06,661
It won't matter.

274
00:18:07,580 --> 00:18:08,410
Super!

275
00:18:08,493 --> 00:18:09,323
Nothing will work.

276
00:18:09,460 --> 00:18:11,940
We'll chop you up down to nuts and bolts.

277
00:18:18,940 --> 00:18:21,120
Behold the spinning weapon of death.

278
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:24,100
Sickle girl, go!

279
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:35,680
Okay, I'll give you props.

280
00:18:36,580 --> 00:18:38,857
It's not every day
someone's got enough power

281
00:18:38,940 --> 00:18:41,337
to punch a hole through the general body.

282
00:18:41,420 --> 00:18:43,900
But I gotta say, what you're trying to do,

283
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:47,569
it's like a praying man that's
looking to sink a battleship.

284
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:53,517
You're in for a treat, the thousand
sun will come in a whole sea one day,

285
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:54,430
but in the.

286
00:18:54,513 --> 00:18:55,797
In the meantime, I want
to give you a taste.

287
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:57,597
of this ultimate secret weapon.

288
00:18:57,680 --> 00:19:00,739
Don't tell anybody else
though, cause it's a secret.

289
00:19:02,940 --> 00:19:06,740
The land-based portal gallon cannon.

290
00:19:09,220 --> 00:19:12,897
The working title is...

291
00:19:12,980 --> 00:19:14,140
Take it!

292
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:23,060
Shenron King!

293
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:28,320
Still don't know who this guy is!

294
00:19:28,660 --> 00:19:32,580
Or why he's so hell-bent on
keeping up from retrieving Caesar!

295
00:19:40,100 --> 00:19:42,080
Who's that passed out down there?

296
00:19:42,340 --> 00:19:43,460
Looks like Caesar.

297
00:19:45,940 --> 00:19:48,234
Wonder how he got all the way out here.

298
00:19:52,060 --> 00:19:54,020
It don't matter who's paying you.

299
00:19:54,260 --> 00:19:57,142
We're not gonna get our
asses kicked that easily.

300
00:19:58,100 --> 00:19:58,930
Well, well.

301
00:19:59,100 --> 00:20:00,257
Still standing, huh?

302
00:20:00,340 --> 00:20:02,097
Gotta admit you're tough, for real.

303
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:05,360
If you think we're just your
garden-variety hooligans,

304
00:20:05,540 --> 00:20:07,537
pal, you're gonna get a rude awakening!

305
00:20:07,620 --> 00:20:08,560
We swear!

306
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:09,917
By the name of Joker!

307
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,360
We're taking Caesar! You hear me?

308
00:20:12,540 --> 00:20:13,940
You won't stop us!

309
00:20:14,700 --> 00:20:15,530
Ah!

310
00:20:15,613 --> 00:20:17,480
So your plan is finally revealed!

311
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:20,197
You guys are trying to escape with Caesar!

312
00:20:20,280 --> 00:20:21,860
I see a light up ahead!

313
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:26,560
Keep the wind going, Nami! More!

314
00:20:27,020 --> 00:20:29,540
It's gonna be a world of poison outside!

315
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:46,900
You've seen what I've seen!

316
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:50,160
The general's so cool! What?

317
00:20:52,040 --> 00:20:52,870
Super!

318
00:20:54,300 --> 00:20:55,240
It's a super!

319
00:20:55,780 --> 00:20:56,740
With a good toy!

320
00:21:00,860 --> 00:21:01,690
Buffalo.

321
00:21:01,773 --> 00:21:04,320
Baby Five, what are you doing here? Us?

322
00:21:04,520 --> 00:21:08,873
And what do you think you're doing
helping the Straw Hats and kids escape?

323
00:21:09,020 --> 00:21:10,357
Because Lost turned traitor.

324
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:14,017
Joker saved the heart seed for
you, and you go and betray him!

325
00:21:14,100 --> 00:21:16,840
Wait, are they your friends or something?

326
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:20,150
Negative.

327
00:21:20,233 --> 00:21:21,100
They're my enemies.

328
00:21:29,340 --> 00:21:32,477
All of the Straw Hats in the
Navy Team Five against us?

329
00:21:32,560 --> 00:21:33,777
Those are losing odds.

330
00:21:33,860 --> 00:21:34,742
We gotta split!

331
00:21:35,040 --> 00:21:37,400
Wait, Baby Five, what's going on?

332
00:21:37,540 --> 00:21:39,800
Why are you here? Saving you.

333
00:21:39,980 --> 00:21:42,017
We're taking you to the young master.

334
00:21:42,100 --> 00:21:44,477
They grabbed Caesar and made a run for it.

335
00:21:44,560 --> 00:21:46,031
You know what that means.

336
00:21:46,180 --> 00:21:48,480
It's a sniper's job to take him down.

337
00:21:50,640 --> 00:21:51,477
Those bastards...

338
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:52,390
Hold up, Law.

339
00:21:53,540 --> 00:21:56,197
Usopp said he's got a handle
on the situation, didn't he?

340
00:21:56,280 --> 00:21:57,620
First class sniper.

341
00:21:57,840 --> 00:21:59,237
Don't underestimate him.

342
00:21:59,320 --> 00:22:00,150
You're crazy.

343
00:22:00,233 --> 00:22:01,237
What if he misses?

344
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:03,457
If Caesar escapes, this
whole planet's ruined.

345
00:22:03,540 --> 00:22:05,422
Are we in alliance or aren't we?

346
00:22:05,680 --> 00:22:09,297
If we're going to work together,
how about showing a little trust?

347
00:22:09,380 --> 00:22:11,600
What alliance? Hang on.

348
00:22:11,820 --> 00:22:12,702
Don't think so.

349
00:22:12,880 --> 00:22:13,880
I'm done waiting.

350
00:22:16,060 --> 00:22:17,600
I went on the offense.

351
00:22:19,340 --> 00:22:20,760
Think you got away?

352
00:22:21,100 --> 00:22:22,580
Think again, cowards!

353
00:22:22,780 --> 00:22:24,300
You're all going down!

354
00:22:25,620 --> 00:22:26,540
That's right!

355
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:29,117
Especially when they're wounded
and their backs are to us!

356
00:22:29,200 --> 00:22:30,030
Too easy!

357
00:22:35,480 --> 00:22:37,060
Yeah, any day.

358
00:22:37,780 --> 00:22:39,860
First, you need a little water.

359
00:22:41,740 --> 00:22:43,580
Now, work your magic!

360
00:22:44,540 --> 00:22:45,840
It's time to grow!

361
00:22:46,860 --> 00:22:49,400
Black Kabuto and... Chump grass!

362
00:22:50,800 --> 00:22:51,780
Eat up!

363
00:22:51,920 --> 00:22:53,155
You're gonna need it!

364
00:22:56,780 --> 00:22:58,657
It looks like they're about to attack.

365
00:22:58,740 --> 00:23:02,337
Be careful, buffalo—leave the
flag to me while I'm busy.

366
00:23:02,420 --> 00:23:04,177
You keep the skies clear.

367
00:23:04,260 --> 00:23:05,877
We got a mission to complete.

368
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:06,917
What, Roger?

369
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:10,897
That, my—you really
need me. Don't you then?

370
00:23:10,980 --> 00:23:13,097
I'll be there.

371
00:23:13,180 --> 00:23:15,077
I'll protect you with my life.

372
00:23:15,160 --> 00:23:16,737
Go, high feather egg!

373
00:23:16,820 --> 00:23:18,600
feather egg

374
00:23:20,800 --> 00:23:22,560
Something just flew overhead!

375
00:23:22,840 --> 00:23:23,680
Time to hatch!

376
00:23:24,100 --> 00:23:25,360
Little bolt!

377
00:23:34,600 --> 00:23:36,640
A thunder storm? Buffalo!

378
00:23:37,100 --> 00:23:37,960
We gotta go!

379
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:39,680
I'm trying, I'm trying!

380
00:23:40,060 --> 00:23:41,900
Oh no, not so fast.

381
00:23:44,520 --> 00:23:45,638
Meteorology attack!

382
00:23:47,900 --> 00:23:48,730
Thunderbreed!

383
00:23:50,440 --> 00:23:53,340
No way! Tempo! Stop!

384
00:24:00,520 --> 00:24:03,320
Say something, baby! Damn it!

385
00:24:03,920 --> 00:24:04,980
She's out cold!

386
00:24:08,560 --> 00:24:10,920
Time to wrap this up!

387
00:24:11,120 --> 00:24:12,120
Do it, Jumpgrass!

388
00:24:13,260 --> 00:24:14,440
Special attack!

389
00:24:14,800 --> 00:24:16,500
Meteor Storm Assault!

390
00:24:19,560 --> 00:24:20,390
Buffalo!

391
00:24:20,473 --> 00:24:21,303
I can't move!

392
00:24:21,386 --> 00:24:22,593
Or fly for that matter!

393
00:24:22,780 --> 00:24:24,437
Please, you gotta protect me!

394
00:24:24,520 --> 00:24:27,180
I always perform my duty!

395
00:24:27,680 --> 00:24:30,240
I'm part of the Dachyote family!

396
00:24:30,740 --> 00:24:32,600
The mission above all else!

397
00:24:38,840 --> 00:24:39,940
Lights, idiot!

398
00:24:40,220 --> 00:24:41,437
You're good for nothing!

399
00:24:41,520 --> 00:24:43,777
Go on, try it! I'm gas!

400
00:24:43,860 --> 00:24:45,300
You can't hit me.

401
00:24:47,380 --> 00:24:53,580
Gotta make it to Dressrosa with or without
Buffalo and Baby Five. Nope. Afraid not.

402
00:24:53,820 --> 00:24:54,820
That last shot.

403
00:24:55,840 --> 00:24:57,580
No. What is this?

404
00:24:58,780 --> 00:25:00,720
A sea prism stone handcuff.

405
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:05,120
And that is how it's done.

406
00:25:07,480 --> 00:25:09,380
Yeah, in your face, Caesar.

407
00:25:11,620 --> 00:25:14,097
When the enemy turns
their back, I'm there.

408
00:25:14,180 --> 00:25:15,240
With the enemy?

409
00:25:15,420 --> 00:25:16,361
Yeah, we get it.

410
00:25:25,420 --> 00:25:26,250
Fine.

411
00:25:26,440 --> 00:25:29,087
Looks like the initial
phase is accomplished.

412
00:25:29,780 --> 00:25:30,610
Told you.

413
00:25:30,780 --> 00:25:32,368
Pretty strong, aren't they?

414
00:25:50,140 --> 00:25:53,677
looks like i overslept no big deal

415
00:25:53,760 --> 00:25:58,100
now then which way is punk hazard
